A||||7||loafer87gt||My little buddy is going to be OK!||||10||
Z||000000||loafer87gt||09-12-2001||06:45 PM||||I am so relieved. I just got a call back from the Vetrinarians office and my cat tested negative for the Feline Leukemia disease. She went in yesterday morning for a bunch of bloodwork and urinalysis tests after the vet suspected her to be a afflicted with the illness. It turns out she just has a bladder and gum infection. They have no idea why this is happening (second time in under two months for the bladder infection) so we still have to figure that out. I am so happy to hear this news, I don't know what i would do without my little sidekick. Here is some pictures of Spike. A stray mother cat showed up at my parents place last Christmas, and to make a long story short, they took care of her and she ended up giving birth to about ten kittens. Unfortunately, the mother and all other of the nine kittens had to be put down as they had distemperment. For some reason Spike wasn't affected by the illness, in fact, she isn't even a carrier. I decided to bring Spike back to Saskatoon with me and she has been here since. These are some old pictures, as she is now tipping the scales at over 16 pounds. As my vet set, she's no ballerina!<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.members.shaw.ca/loafer/Misc/spike1.jpg">    <P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.members.shaw.ca/loafer/Misc/spike2.jpg">    <P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.members.shaw.ca/loafer/Misc/spike3.jpg">    <BR><p>[This message has been edited by loafer87gt (edited 09-12-2001).]||||reg||10
